[b]QLC+ Swiss Knife v1.9.0 — one show, every tool[/b]

A new release of Swiss Knife, the free companion toolkit for QLC+ 5 workspaces (not affiliated with the QLC+ project).

Moving a show to a new venue takes many small adjustments across tools, back and forth. Until now each tool wrote its own file; from 1.9 you open the show once and every tool works on it:
[list]
[*][b]The show in progress[/b]: each tool's main button is "Apply to the show"; the header counts the changes and shows the Doctor status; a History lets you undo any step (and redo); one "Save as new file…" writes it all with a report. Your original file is never touched.
[*][b]Function Porter[/b] now also copies fixtures and fixture groups from another show (what the old QXW Merger did), with free-address checks and 3D positions, and ports looks, chasers and their buttons onto them.
[*][b]Show Paperwork[/b]: tech rider for the venue (never carries your show internals), crew checklist for load-in and show book for you, in one tool — combined in one PDF if you like, with a stage plot; A4, A3 or US Letter.
[*][b]Guided routes[/b]: "Adapt a show to a new venue" and "Get ready for the gig" show the steps above the tools — any step, any order.
[*]Every screen laid out the same way, with a "?" to its wiki page; tabs in the Look Builder and Stage & Meshes.
[/list]

Download: [url=https://github.com/giopas/qlc-plus-swiss-knife-tool-script/releases/tag/v1.9.0]GitHub release v1.9.0[/url] · [url=https://github.com/giopas/qlc-plus-swiss-knife-tool-script/wiki]Wiki[/url]
